<title>USA: Sprint to install $60 mln in loop carriers.</title>
<headline>Sprint to install $60 mln in loop carriers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp expects to install an additional $60 million of next-generation digital loop carrier system components throughout its U.S. service areas in the next two years, one of Sprint's loop carrier systems suppliers said.</p>
<p>The supplier, Cleveland-based RELTEC Corp., also said Sprint chose RELTEC's loop carrier system for its U.S. service area.</p>
<p>The company did not put a dollar value on the selection.</p>
<p>Sprint officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
